# Commits the Hyprland plugins are deployed from.
#
# Sourced by two readers that cannot see each other's world:
#
#   - desktop/.config/hypr/scripts/garage-rebuild-plugins, in the user's
#     session, which builds and installs from these commits;
#   - system/bin/kinetik-plugin-hook, as root inside a pacman transaction,
#     which has no checkout and no $HOME to look in and reads the copy
#     bootstrap.sh installs at /usr/lib/kinetik/plugin-pins.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for both. Bumping a plugin means
# editing it here and nowhere else; garage-rebuild-plugins refreshes the
# installed copy from this one whenever the two differ, so the hook cannot end
# up looking for a build of a commit that is no longer pinned.
#
# Format is deliberately plain KEY=VALUE with no expansion, quoting or
# substitution: both readers are POSIX sh and `.` this file directly, so
# anything else here would execute in a root shell inside a pacman transaction.
# Both readers additionally check that each value is a full 40-character hex
# object id before using it.

